# Auto-Spec Development Environment

Create a `.env` file in the project root with your configuration:

```env
# LLM API Keys (choose one)
NVIDIA_API_KEY=your-nvidia-api-key
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-key

# LLM Configuration
LLM_PROVIDER=nvidia
LLM_MODEL=meta/llama-3.1-70b-instruct
LLM_TEMPERATURE=0.2

# Vector Database (optional - uses default paths if not set)
# CHROMA_DB_PATH=/path/to/chroma_db
# CHROMA_DB_REMOTE_URL=https://your-storage-url/chroma_db/

# Embedding Configuration
EMBEDDING_MODEL=BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5

# RAG Configuration
TOP_K_RESULTS=3
SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD=0.3

# Output Configuration
OUTPUT_DIR=./auto_spec_output
```

## Required Environment Variables

At minimum, you need:
- `NVIDIA_API_KEY` OR `OPENAI_API_KEY` (for LLM access)

## Optional Environment Variables

- `CHROMA_DB_REMOTE_URL` - URL to download pre-built vector database
- `LLM_PROVIDER` - LLM provider (default: "nvidia")
- `LLM_MODEL` - LLM model name (default: "meta/llama-3.1-70b-instruct")
- `OUTPUT_DIR` - Directory to save generated specs (default: "./auto_spec_output")

## First Time Setup

1. Copy `.env.example` to `.env`
2. Fill in your API keys
3. Run `auto-spec setup` to download the vector database
4. You're ready to go!
